Subject: Chat Workbench CSP Connect Justification
Date: 2026-05-14
Scope: Browser fetch repair for AlienHand The Lounge to payload resolver communication

& [ChatWorkbenchCSPConnectSlice] is the browser fetch blocker repair after live workbench review
  + [specification_basis] is AlienHand/docs/irc-chat-refinement.sop
  + [processed_specification_basis] is AlienHand/docs/sjs/exploded/irc-chat-refinement.v2.exploded.sop
  + [review_basis] is user report that AlienHand refinement API fetch failed for /blocks persisted after CORS hardening
  + [diagnosis] is resolver CORS passed direct and preflight requests, but The Lounge Content-Security-Policy blocked browser fetch because connect-src omitted the AlienHand resolver origin
  + [thelounge_commit] is ff420428
  + [parent_pointer] is AlienHand/thelounge
  + [implementation_files] are The Lounge server/server.ts and AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/payload_http.py

  = observed: current live The Lounge returned Content-Security-Policy connect-src 'self' ws: wss:
  = observed: current live resolver returned Access-Control-Allow-Origin for The Lounge, Access-Control-Allow-Private-Network true, and valid preflight response
  = inferred: browser Failed to fetch persisted because CSP prevented the cross-origin resolver request before the successful CORS response could be used
  = implemented: The Lounge server now adds Config.values.alienhand.payloadResolverBaseUrl origin to connect-src when AlienHand supplies a resolver
  = implemented: non-http and invalid resolver values are ignored for CSP safety
  = implemented: AlienHand runtime group proof now requires The Lounge CSP to include the resolver origin
  = implemented: AlienHand workbench runtime proof now requires The Lounge CSP to include the resolver origin

  = satisfies: ChatWorkbenchLiveReviewCorrectionsSlice because successful source insertion depends on browser access to /blocks and /cuts endpoints
  = satisfies: UIInteractionSpecification because the visible row arrow can only complete its intended action when browser fetch to the refinement API is permitted
  = satisfies: DataDrivenDesign because the resolver origin remains derived from the launched app-owned resolver identity instead of hard-coded ports
